# Agentic Runs Terminology Rule

## CRITICAL: The Terminology Has Changed — "Plans" Is Deprecated

The entire AI Hub feature set has migrated away from the "plans" naming convention.
Any use of deprecated terms in **user-facing UI strings** (labels, headings, breadcrumbs, button text, aria-labels,
toast messages, empty-state copy) is a **regression bug**.

---

## Banned User-Facing Terms (non-v3 files)

| ❌ BANNED | ✅ USE INSTEAD |
|---|---|
| `Agentic plans` | `Agentic runs` |
| `Agentic plan` | `Agentic run` |
| `Troubleshooting plans` | `Agentic runs` |
| `Troubleshooting plan` | `Agentic run` |
| `Plan details` | `Run details` |
| `plan detail` (in breadcrumbs/titles) | `run detail` |
| `Deny plan` | `Deny run` |

### Legitimate Uses (do NOT change these)

- **`pages/ai-hub-v3/`** — this is the foundational shared library (fleet inventory bars, cluster
  summaries, audit/log tab, plan simulation types) that the v2 workspace's own components import
  from directly. It is not a standalone routed page anymore, but its internal identifiers/strings
  may still say "plan" — leave those alone unless a specific user-visible string leaks through v2.
- **Internal code identifiers** like variable names (`planId`, `planDomain`, `planSlug`),
  function names, TypeScript type names, CSS class names, and URL path segments (`/troubleshooting-plans/`).
  Only user-visible strings are in scope.
- **"Stop analysis"** — this refers to halting the AI analysis *operation*, not the "plan" entity.
  It is correct terminology for the Analyzing state and should NOT be changed.
- **"remediation plan"** in body copy that describes a multi-step remediation strategy document
  (as opposed to the agentic run entity itself) — context dependent, use judgment.

---

## How to Audit Before Every Edit

Before writing or editing any user-visible string in these prototype directories:

```
src/app/prototypes/ai-hub-autonomous-agentic-plans-mvp/pages/
src/app/prototypes/observability-agentic-troubleshooting-ai/pages/
```

Run this command and confirm zero results:

```bash
rg -n "Plan details|Agentic plans\b|Troubleshooting plans\b|Troubleshooting plan:" \
  src/app/prototypes/ai-hub-autonomous-agentic-plans-mvp/pages/ \
  src/app/prototypes/observability-agentic-troubleshooting-ai/pages/ \
  -g "*.tsx" -g "*.ts" | grep -v "/ai-hub-v3/"
```

**Zero results = clean.** Any result outside the `ai-hub-v3/` path is a bug that must be fixed
before the change is committed.

---

## History: v1 Baseline and Legacy Bridge Pages Have Been Removed

As of 2026-07-20, the `ai-hub-autonomous-agentic-plans-mvp` prototype supports **only the v2
workspace** (`/v2/ai-hub/observe/*`, backed by `pages/v2/` and `pages/ai-hub-plans-v2/`). The
following were permanently deleted because they were the actual root cause of prior recurring
"deprecated UI randomly appears" regressions — a duplicate, non-versioned nav track
(`/core/observe/ai-hub/plans`, `/core/observe/troubleshooting-plans`, etc.) was live in the
sidebar at all times, alongside the v2 nav group, and pointed at stale "plan" terminology pages:

- `pages/v1/`, `pages/ai-hub-v1/` — the frozen "v1.0 — Option B" baseline and its banner version
  picker (`prototype.config.bannerVersionPicker`).
- `pages/AIHubPage.tsx`, `pages/TroubleshootingPlansPage.tsx`, `pages/AuditAndLogsPage.tsx`,
  `pages/PlanRemediationPage.tsx`, `pages/AcsPlanDetailPage.tsx`, `pages/TroubleshootingPlanDetail.tsx`,
  `pages/PlanDetailVersionRouter.tsx` — the non-versioned "bridge" pages built on `ai-hub-v3`.

Their routes now live only as `<BridgeRedirect>` entries in `routes.tsx` (see `pages/BridgeRedirect.tsx`)
so that old bookmarks/cross-links still resolve, redirecting straight to the equivalent `/v2/ai-hub/...`
path. **Do not recreate a second, non-versioned copy of any Agentic runs page.** If a new entry point
into this feature is needed, route it directly to a `v2/` page.

